virglrenderer: Venus vkCmd* indices, counts and offsets stay inside what they name

What: before the Mac's driver records a command, vkr bounds the guest's
indices, counts, offsets, strides and enum values: viewports, scissors, vertex
buffers, color attachment state and sample locations against the device's
limits (first + count, 64-bit); push constants against maxPushConstantsSize;
buffer offsets and ranges of binds, copies, fills, updates, indirect draws and
dispatches, conditional rendering and barriers against the buffer's size;
mip levels and layers of copies, blits, resolves, clears and image barriers
against the image; queries against the pool's count (query pools: a type the
device has, 1 to 2^20 queries; vkGetQueryPoolResults' stride against dataSize);
enum values that index the drivers' tables (bind points, index types, cull
modes, compare and stencil ops, topologies, logic ops, blend factors and ops,
sample counts); command buffer levels: only a primary executes secondaries,
and VK_EXT_nested_command_buffer is hidden; vkCmdDrawMulti(Indexed)EXT gets
its entries' own size as the stride (the decoder packs them). vkr keeps the
device's limits once per physical device (struct vkr_limits), a command
buffer's level, a pipeline's bind point and a query pool's type and count. A
refused command ends the app's context with a log line (the guest records and
creates these without waiting); the decoder stops there.
Why: KosmicKrisp is built with NDEBUG, so Mesa's and its own asserts on these
are gone: a guest index or offset is a host memory access (push constants at
push + offset, SET_DYN_ARRAY at first, vertex buffers and descriptor sets at
firstBinding/firstSet, query reports at firstQuery, vk_meta_clear's stack
array at colorAttachment, a secondary that executes itself recurses until the
stack ends), and an enum value its switch does not know reaches
__builtin_unreachable(). Metal ends the process on level and layer ranges
(newLevelRange). MoltenVK grows a vector to offset + size in 32 bits for push
constants and reads query results past the pool. Probed on Apple7 (M1 Max):
SIGBUS/SIGSEGV/SIGABRT in 3 of 3 runs on the probed cases (ADR 0065).
Upstream: OmacVM policy (the spec makes these the app's job), as #623's image
limits; vkCmdDrawMulti's stride and the nested-recursion are vkr/Mesa bugs on
every host (draft only, not posted).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the c- and q- cases): each refused
case ends its child before the patch (or reaches the driver) and only its
context after it; the legal maxima (every limit at its advertised value) work.
Run on KosmicKrisp, MoltenVK and MoltenVK with prefilled Metal command
buffers (encoding at vkEndCommandBuffer, what QEMU's submit does); --time: us
per vkCmdPushConstants, vkCmdSetViewport and vkCmdDraw through vkr.

